Beryllium is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3
only (SPDX identifier GPL-3.0-only). The licence text is
LICENSES/GPL-3.0-only. Every source file carries an SPDX licence
identifier line naming its licence and a copyright line naming the
responsible human copyright holder, James Morris.

One file is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 only
(SPDX identifier GPL-2.0-only; the text is LICENSES/GPL-2.0-only):
mvp/guest/mgmt/be-mgmt.c, a guest kernel module built against Linux as a
test input of the MVP's `anchor` scenario. It is not part of the monitor
and is never linked into it.

The MVP guests' userland is built from two external inputs, never
committed: BusyBox, licensed GPL-2.0-only (LICENSES/GPL-2.0-only), and
musl, licensed MIT (the text, as musl ships it, is LICENSES/MIT). The
guest build fetches their pinned upstream releases (mvp/guest/pins.txt)
and builds them under build/; no project code is linked into either, and
no guest image is distributed.

mvp/docs/licence-manifest.md, which mvp/tools/licence-manifest.py
generates from the pins, names every component of the MVP's guest
software and of the firmware below it, each with its licence, its notice
text, and its corresponding source. Besides the above: Linux, licensed
GPL-2.0-only WITH Linux-syscall-note (the exception's text is in the
pinned Linux source); nolibc, Linux's minimal C library, which the
guest's init is built against, licensed LGPL-2.1 OR MIT (the LGPL-2.1
text, as Linux ships it, is LICENSES/LGPL-2.1); OpenSBI, licensed
BSD-2-Clause (the text, as OpenSBI v1.6 ships it, is
LICENSES/BSD-2-Clause); and U-Boot, licensed GPL-2.0-or-later (its GPL
version 2 text, as U-Boot v2022.10 ships it, is
LICENSES/GPL-2.0-or-later). None is committed, and the MVP distributes no
binary of any.

The licence texts under LICENSES/ are in the Linux kernel's form
(Valid-License-Identifier, SPDX-URL, Usage-Guide, License-Text).
mvp/tools/check-licenses.py, run by `./mvp/mvp check`, requires that every
identifier a tracked file's header names, a `source` line of the guest
pins names for an external input, or a `licence` line of the licence
manifest names, has its text under LICENSES/ and is named in this file.
